# Onboarding — Agent-Driven Development in {{REPO_NAME}}

Welcome! This repo uses **CraftKit**: instead of asking a coding agent to
"just build it", work flows through phases — each producing a reviewable
artifact, each gated by *you*. The agent never guesses; when it's unsure, it
asks you structured questions and waits.

## Day one

1. Open your agent harness in the repo root — any of these works the same way:
   - **Claude Code** — `claude`
   - **pi** — `pi`
   - **GitHub Copilot CLI** — `copilot`
2. Run `/ck-onboard`. It walks you through the modules, the pipeline, and a
   toy ticket end-to-end (~20 minutes, touches no source code).

## Day-to-day commands

| You want to… | Run |
|--------------|-----|
| Build a feature | `/ck-feature` |
| Fix a bug (have a trace/error?) | `/ck-bugfix` |
| Review your branch before a PR | `/ck-review` |
| Update dependencies | `/ck-deps` |
| Run a single phase (resume mid-pipeline) | `/ck-requirements`, `/ck-tech-spec`, `/ck-execution-plan`, `/ck-implement`, `/ck-ship`, … |

Every workflow pauses at each phase and shows you a summary with options.
Nothing advances without your approval; nothing is pushed without `ship`.

## When the agent escalates

This is normal and good — it means the agent refused to guess.

1. Open `artifacts/{TICKET}/escalations/{phase}.md`
2. Each question has **Context** (why it matters) and **Impact** (what it
   unblocks). Replace each `<!-- PENDING -->` with your answer.
3. Re-run the same command. Your answers may resolve everything or raise
   follow-ups (a new round in the same file) — keep answering until it
   proceeds.

## Where everything lives

| Path | What it is |
|------|-----------|
| `artifacts/{TICKET}/` | The paper trail: requirements → tech spec → plan → review per ticket. Read a finished ticket's directory to see how the team decomposes work. |
| `.craftkit-project/project.yaml` | Module registry, build commands, ticket format, protected files |
| `.craftkit-project/context/` | Workspace summary + per-module coding patterns |
| `.craftkit/` | The vendored kit (skills + workflows). Don't edit — it's replaced on `craftkit update`. |
| `AGENTS.md` | The rules every harness loads |

## Learning the codebase through the pipeline

- Browse completed `artifacts/{TICKET}/` directories — each is a worked
  example: what was asked, how it was designed, how it was reviewed.
- Read `escalations/` files in those tickets — they record the questions
  experts asked and the decisions made, with reasoning.
- Approve gates slowly at first: read each artifact before choosing
  "proceed". That review *is* the training.
